label act1_day13:
    scene bg black
    "Sunday"
    scene bg black
    m "Hey [player]! Thanks for having me over."
    m "It's nice having just the two of us here...alone..."
    m "This IS what you wanted, right? To be alone with me?"
    n "Or was it me?"
    s "Or me?"
    y "Or me?"
    "The next thing I know, I'm being held down to my chair by each of the girls."
    mc "Wha- what are you doing?"
    "Monika/Sayori: Exactly what you wanted..."
    "Natsuki/Yuri: Keeping you away..."
    qu "From me..."
    "A familiar silhouette approaches."
    qu "It's exactly what I thought. You just cling to any girl who gives you attention. "
    qu "Showing no thought of your own. What were you before me?"
    "I try to answer, but no words come out. "
    "I scream, but only silence is the result of my hoarse throat. "
    "As I look up, the silhouette disperses and Elsea is standing above me, towering over me looking down as if I was a bug."
    "Elsea: That's correct! without me...you're nothing!"
    scene bg bedroom
    "My eyes shoot open as I wake up."
    mc "Agh...Dammit..."
    "There I go thinking I was over her. Who am I kidding? "
    "It's been two weeks and I've done nothing but sulk or find distractions. "
    "And everything I've done so far has been because of them."
    "And I can't stop thinking about what Sayori and Natsuki said yesterday about Monika and I going together."
    " While it's easy to write off Natsuki as just teasing for shits and giggles, Sayori has been tiptoeing around the same thing for the past week. "
    "I mean, it's not a bad thought. And I'd be lying if I didn't admit I haven't wondered if we had gotten together beforehand, but our worlds are just too far apart now. "
    "And I don't want her to grow to hate me. Not until I-"
    "*GGRRWLLLL*" #[Stomach Growling Sound]"
    mc "Oh yeah. Food."
    scene bg living_room_morning
    "After washing up and heading downstairs to make a quick breakfast, I realize that it's only 6:54."
    "Man, yesterday threw my sleep schedule off. "
    "At least it's a positive shift this time. "
    "I've got a few hours so..."
    "I find the remote and open up a streaming site. "
    "As soon as I'm on my profile and begin flipping through the recommendations..."
    mc "Wow. I really didn't have a personality without her."
    "Nothing but rom coms and chick flicks. "
    "At this point, I might as well delete my profile and start all over. "
    "As I hover over the delete option, I hesitate."
    mc "Eh. I barely watch anything anyway."
    "I walk over to pick up a controller and turn a game on, but as I'm flipping through them..."
    mc "Nothing but multiplayer or co-op. *Sigh*"
    "I pick something that I feel I can eat some time, but after about 15 minutes, I'm already getting bored of it. "
    "I set the controller down thinking about what I can even do to pass the time. "
    "As I sit back and think, my mind goes back to my dream. All the girls have helped keep my mind off Elsea. "
    "From the club, to the poems and the books-"
    mc "That's it!"
    "I run over to the closet and take out my book bag and retrieve the copy of Portrait of Markov Yuri lent to me. "
    "I walk over to the couch and sit down as I begin to read."
    scene bg living_room_morning
    with dissolve
    "When I noticed I'm about half way done with the book, I stop to check the time. "
    "10:22."
    mc "She did say 10am, right?"
    "I check my messages and sure enough, yup. 10am. Huh. I wonder what's taking he-"
    mc "I DIDN'T SEND HER MY ADDRESS DID I?"
    "Crap crap crap! I call Monika, hoping to catch her in time to apologize."
    "*riing* *riing*"
    m "Hello?"
    mc "Monika! Hey, [player]. Sorry, I just realized, I never gave you my address. "
    mc "Figured you may have been waiting for that looking at the time. I can send it know if that oka-"
    m "Oh, no worries. I know where you live."
    "..."
    mc "...What."
    m "Hee hee. sorry, I just realized how creepy that sounded. I've been to Sayori's house before, so I know my way."
    mc "Oh. Yeah. That...makes sense."
    m "I was about to be on time until I realized I forgot my laptop charger, so I had to double back to get it. I'm about 5 minutes out. Sorry to make you worry."
    mc "Oh, it's no biggie. Yeah. See you soon."
    m "See you soon~"
    "As I hang up, I expect to be calming down, but the anxiety keeps building. "
    "It's not like I haven't had girls over. It's just...none like THE Monika. "
    "The class star. "
    "The object of every guy's eye...which is exactly why Sayori and Natsuki are crazy thinking she has any feeling more than friendship with me."
    "Right. Just friends. Just..."
    "*DING DONG*" #[Doorbell Sound]"
    "That's her! "
    "Okay. Calm down. You got this. "
    "You got this."
    scene bg front_door_morning
    "I open the door to see Monika looking at the address and her phone."
    m "Oh, good. I thought I went to the wrong side of Sayori for a second."
    "I stand there and slightly gawk at Monika's outfit. "
    "If this is her casual, then her formal attire must be top notch."
    mc "Ah...yeah! Hi! Umm...come in."
    "I hold my hand out to guide her way like I'm some sort of butler as she walks in giggling."
    m "Well, I see you're quite the host."
    mc "Oh, uh. Thanks."
    scene bg living_room_morning
    "Monika walks into the living room to sit, looking around taking everything in."
    mc "Uh, Do you need a drink? I can get you aaaaaaa..."
    "Crap! What do I have? "
    "Let's see...lukewarm bottle water and sparkling water in the pantry. What's in the fridge?"
    "..."
    "..."
    "DAMMIT! I can't remember since I had to move stuff for the cupcakes! Maybe I can-"
    m "I've never had it, but I can try it since you're so persistent about it."
    mc "... Wha?"
    m "The 'Aaaaaa'. I can try that if you don't mind."
    "I stare at Monika in confusion until she starts giggling. "
    "Then it hits me that I stalled on the word 'a' while stuck in thought."
    "Gah!!! I'm such a fricking goober!"
    mc "Eh heh. Good one. I kinda had a brain fart trying to remember what I actually had. "
    mc "All that's in my memory is the cupcakes."
    m "Oh yeah! Natsuki told me you two made good work with those. "
    m "She even had a compliment or two about your part."
    mc "Really? Huh. I'm surprised she said something good about me."
    m "Well, she did frame it as a compliment to herself. She basically compared it to training a dog."
    mc "That's...not surprising."
    m "Do you mind if I take a look at the cupcakes?"
    mc "Depends. Are you sure you're not working for Sayori?"
    m "Hee hee. I promise there will be no heist of baked goods."
    mc "In that case, by all means."
    "Monika gets up and opens the fridge."
    m "You two did a wonderful job! These look delicious. Hmm..."
    "I lean over and see Monika trying to open one of the containers."
    mc "Uh, what are you doing?"
    m "Just getting a closer look."
    mc "I mean, they all look the same. I just don't want any to get ruined."
    m "I'll be as careful as possible. But if my finger just so happens to accidentally get frosting on it while inspecting..."
    "Monika winks at me in her coy way that always gets me blushing. "
    "I start rubbing the back of my neck, unable to think of a response."
    m "Hee hee, I was just teasing, [player]. I know Natsuki takes pride in her work and I wouldn't want to ruin anything for her."
    mc "Yeah. Of course. I-I knew that. Welp! We should probably get started."
    "I have no idea what's going on. How is she so calm in this situation? "
    "My nerves are all over the place, but she's just so natural..."
    "Right. Because it's just like I thought. To her, it's like a visit with any other friend. "
    "Like Natsuki, Sayori, and Yuri. No different."
    m "So, do you have the printer down here somewhere or-"
    mc "Oh. It's upstairs. I can bring it down here real quick. It's not that heavy."
    m "Hmm. I'm surprised. Most other guys would jump at the chance of inviting me upstairs."
    "I freeze. Calm down. She's just teasing. "
    "Just like she said. Just pretend like it's Natsuki or Sayori."
    mc "I mean, If you wanna go upstairs, we can. Whatever makes you comfortable."
    "That catches Monika off guard as she begins to blush."
    m "Umm. Down here is fine. Yup. Enough room here to work."
    "I flash a sly smile to her."
    mc "I was just teasing Monika. You really fluster easily."
    "Monika begins to pout and then softly smiles."
    m "I'll admit, you got me. Fine. Let's call a truce on the teasing, okay?"
    mc "Deal."
    m "Besides, I don't want to give you any ideas since we're all alone."
    mc "What the- I thought you said-"
    m "Starting now!"
    "I open my mouth and just close it as Monika hums to herself looking around like she's completely innocent."
    "I head upstairs to go grab the printer while trying to keep my composure."
    #"[Office room]"
    "I...was not expecting to be in a flirt off with her, but it's done."
    "I hope. "
    "The odds are definitely stacked against me if she starts back up again. "
    "I should probably try to focus on the job at hand and get it done to avoid any other awkward situations."
    scene bg living_room_morning
    "I arrive back in the living room to see Monika has already made a workspace and has her laptop out and ready." 
    "She moved the coffee table closer to the couch for easy reach."
    mc "I see you made yourself comfortable."
    m "Oh, sorry. I figured I could at least get the area set up. "
    m "Wow! That's the printer you had? That's larger than I thought."
    mc "That's what sh-"
    "Nope!"
    mc "I mean, that's what aaa..."
    "Monika starts giggling."
    m "It's okay. Those jokes don't phase me. I kinda set you up for that one."
    mc "Heh heh...sorry."
    m "Hey, you're at home. No need to feel uneasy. Relax."
