    mc "Sorry, I was just...sorry."
    "I scoot away to the far end of the couch."
    m "If you were my friend, I wouldn't have minded. But as you said, I am just your class president."
    mc "Wait...no Monika, I didn't mean it like-"
    m "But you're acting like that. I can tell you're uncomfortable." 
    m "I thought a few jokes here and there would help lighten the mood, but..."
    mc "I'm sorry. I do see you as a friend. A good friend."
    mc "It's just, a bit of a weird thing for me to still wrap my head around other people here with me who aren't my folks or Els-"
    "I freeze."
    "Monika chuckles."
    m "Of course that's it. I'm...sorry. I was a bit selfish there and..I understand."
    m "But I don't want you forcing anything with me. "
    m "If me being here makes you uncomfortable then-"
    mc "No! It's not that. I do enjoy your company. It's just..."
    m "It's...fine. Really. Let's just focus on the task at hand, okay?"
    mc "Yeah. Okay."
    "She continues to move around on her laptop as I sit then and watch her. She glances over at me and smiles."
    m "I wouldn't mind a second pair of eyes on this before we print."
    "She scoots towards me while turning the laptop in my direction. I scoot closer to take a look and go over what she has."
    mc "Wow. This is amazing! When did you find time to do this?"
    m "It wasn't easy, but was definitely worth it. "
    m "Any issues? Anything you notice that could be different or better?"
    mc "I've got nothing. You nailed it."
    m "Glad you think so! And here...are the reading suggestions!"
    "I look at it and just like the others, the layout looks masterful."
    mc "Great as well! I might need a copy of this for myself."
    m "Before I print this one, did you have any suggestions? "
    m "As you can see, we've also added some manga titles, so feel free to suggest some."
    mc "Oh, no. Thanks though. I don't think I have anything that matches what you guys already had."
    "Monika begins to frown again."
    m "*Sigh* I was afraid you'd say something like that. "
    m "You know, just because we were in the club longer, doesn't make you worse than us. Your opinions matter too."
    scene bg black
    "Elsea: ... Showing no thought of your own. What were you before me?"
    scene bg living_room
    mc "I...I'm okay with...what you already have. I haven't read anything lately, so I don't really have any suggestions to begin with."
    "Monika frowns at me as she takes the laptop back."
    m "Okay...let's just see how these come out."
    "She prints a copy of each one and then folds them."
    m "Huh. These should work just fine."
    mc "Yeah. They look great."
