    "I turn to her and can see she's getting into a deep headspace. I can't stand to see her like this."
    mc "Sorry. That's personal. I'll take your word that you'll manage."
    m "It's...okay. I just don't want you worrying too much. You have enough to worry about as is."
    "We both sit in an awkward silence. I really do want to open up to her, but with all that's going on, I'd hate to be a distraction."
    m "Listen, [player]. About Friday. I want to-"
    mc "I know, and I'm sorry. I should've spoken up more to the rumors. I'm sure me rejecting them will get it to stop."
    m "That's not what-"
    "*BEEP BEEP*" # [Beeping Sound]"
    "Monica: Huh? What happened?"
    "I walk over to the printer to check the display." 
    "Cyan out."
    mc "It's okay. It just needs new ink. Just a moment."
    "I head upstairs to grab replacement cartridges for all of them just in case."
    "As I come back down, I see Monika on her phone texting."
    m "Well, Sayori and Yuri are done with the decorations."
    mc "Really? With them too, I'm surprised they came to a stopping point. "
    mc "I know how much of a runaway train Sayori can be when she sets her mind to it."
    m "Yeah. She's really persistent like that..."
    mc "Hey, can I ask you something?"
    m "Sure. Go ahead."
    mc "I've been kinda...worried about Sayori. "
    mc "There are days where she seems a bit out of it. "
    mc "I'm no expert, but I'm not convinced that it is a normal 'womanly problem'"
    "Monika begins to look away and twiddle with her phone in her hand."
